  "note": "Election of twelve members of the Downpatrick Urban Council, January 1929. Thirteen nominations were lodged; the withdrawal of Mr. Joseph Black left twelve candidates for twelve seats and there was no contest. Seven Nationalists and five Unionists returned unopposed. Mr. J. Black (Nationalist) withdrew. Returned unopposed."
